+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every tool registered in `ToolRegistry` declares a JSON Schema in `definition.inputSchema` that providers forward to the model, and `ToolRegistry.execute` enforces that same schema before the tool's executor runs. A call whose input violates `required`, a declared property `type`, or `enum` returns a `ToolResponse` describing the failing property paths and constraints rather than throwing, so the orchestrator sends the rejection back to the model as a `tool_result` within its existing `DEFAULT_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS = 5` loop budget instead of aborting the turn.
+
+## Validation contract
+
+- `execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before calling the executor, rejecting missing required fields, wrong property types, and invalid enum values with a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the failing field path and expected constraint without invoking the executor, without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types, or applying defaults so valid input with extra properties passes through unchanged, and without leaking any rejected property value into the returned text or any log line ([validated by: rejects malformed input without calling the executor or leaking field values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L13)).
+- Calling `execute` with an unregistered tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`; only schema validation failures become a returned `ToolResponse`.
+
+## Schema compilation
+
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time; an uncompilable schema causes `register` to throw synchronously with a message that names the tool, so a broken schema fails at startup rather than mid-conversation ([validated by: throws at register time when a static inputSchema is uncompilable, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L77)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves per call and validates against the schema returned for that call, never a stale schema from an earlier call ([validated by: validates a function-valued tool definition against the schema returned for that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L89)).
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled once at registration and reused across subsequent `execute` calls rather than recompiled on every invocation.
+
+## Orchestrator integration
+
+- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` rather than throwing, `createChatOrchestrator` delivers the rejection text to the provider in the next round's `tool_result` message and resolves `processMessage` once the model retries with valid input, bounded by `DEFAULT_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS = 5` ([validated by: delivers a validation rejection as a tool_result so a corrected retry succeeds](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L128)).
